Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This notice lists the third-party components Runfree redistributes or installs,
so recipients can find the licenses that apply to them. It records what is
bundled and where each component's license text lives. It is not legal advice
and it is not a clearance opinion.

Three distribution surfaces carry third-party code, and they are not the same
set:

1. The `runfree` executable in the release archive
2. The container images Runfree builds on the user's machine
3. The repository's development dependencies, which ship in neither of the above

1. The `runfree` executable
---------------------------

The release archive contains a single executable compiled with Bun. It embeds
the Bun runtime and the JavaScript dependencies the CLI imports.

  Bun                     MIT (with bundled components under their own terms;
                          see https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/blob/main/LICENSE.md)
  @clack/prompts          MIT
  yargs                   MIT, with its transitive dependencies
  smol-toml               BSD-3-Clause

Each package's license text is in its directory under `node_modules/` in a
source checkout, and in the published package on npm.

2. Container images
-------------------

Runfree builds the agent and proxy images on the user's machine from the pinned
inputs in `packages/agent-runtime/runtime-inputs.lock.json`. These images are
not published as release artifacts today. Anyone who publishes prebuilt Runfree
images takes on the redistribution obligations of everything inside them, which
this notice does not enumerate at the package level.

  Base image            Ubuntu, pinned by digest. Ubuntu packages carry their
                        own licenses, recorded under /usr/share/doc in the image.
  Installed packages    The APT package set pinned in runtime-inputs.lock.json
                        (bash, ca-certificates, curl, git, jq, nftables, nodejs,
                        npm, ripgrep, zsh, and others), under their Debian/Ubuntu
                        licenses.
  GitHub CLI            MIT, installed from the pinned release .deb.
  uv                    Apache-2.0 or MIT, from the pinned ghcr.io image.
  mockttp               Apache-2.0 (proxy image)
  read-tls-client-hello Apache-2.0 (proxy image)

Runfree also installs coding-agent CLIs (Claude Code, Codex, Pi) into the agent
image at pinned versions. Those are the vendors' own products under the vendors'
own terms. Runfree does not relicense them, and using them requires an account
with the respective vendor.

3. Development dependencies
---------------------------

TypeScript, Biome, Vitest, tsx, and the other devDependencies in `package.json`
are build- and test-time only. They are not part of the release archive or the
container images.
